  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "convergence",
    "affected_api": "sklearn.cluster.KMeans",
    "observed_behavior": "KMeans with lloyd or elkan keeps iterating after inertia reaches 0.0 when there are more centers than distinct samples. The log shows Iteration 0 with inertia 40.0, then Iteration 1 through Iteration 299 all with inertia 0.0, and it only stops because max_iter (300 by default) is reached. With max_iter=10_000 it runs as an infinite loop.",
    "expected_behavior": "The algorithm should stop once inertia becomes 0, after Iteration 1 with inertia 0.0. Only 1 iteration should be performed (Iteration 0 and Iteration 1 logged).",
    "manifestation": "hang",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "n_clusters is greater than the number of distinct (non-duplicate) samples in X, e.g. n_clusters=6 on data with 5 distinct points",
      "algorithm is 'lloyd' or 'elkan'",
      "max_iter is large (e.g. 10_000) or infinite, so the loop does not stop at the default 300",
      "empty-cluster relocation triggers on every iteration because all samples sit at distance 0 from their centers"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "KMeans(n_clusters=6, init=init, random_state=0, verbose=True, algorithm='lloyd', max_iter=10_000).fit(X), where X has 5 distinct points and init is a user-supplied array",
        "buggy_output": "Initialization complete; Iteration 0, inertia 40.0.; Iteration 1, inertia 0.0.; Iteration 2, inertia 0.0. ... continues with inertia 0.0 for every iteration, up to Iteration 299 at max_iter=300"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": []
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": "inertia drops from 40.0 at iteration 0 to 0.0 from iteration 1 onward; the run would otherwise continue to max_iter=300",
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Log shows inertia 40.0 at Iteration 0 then 0.0 at Iteration 1 through 299, with run hitting the 300-iteration default cap rather than converging",
      "ConvergenceWarning: Number of distinct clusters (5) found smaller than n_clusters (6), possibly due to duplicate points in X",
      "Issue reporter expects KMeans should stop at the second iteration because inertia is 0.0",
      "Cause per PR body: when there are more centers than non-duplicate samples, relocation of empty clusters triggers every iteration, preventing the algorithm from stopping",
      "Fix in _average_centers relocates empty clusters to the location of the biggest cluster instead of leaving them at the origin",
      "Regression test test_relocating_with_duplicates uses X=[[0,0],[1,1],[1,1],[1,0],[0,1]] with n_clusters=5, expects warning 'Number of distinct clusters (4) found smaller than n_clusters (5)' and asserts km.n_iter_ == 1, for algorithms lloyd and elkan",
      "Commit message mentions a fast exit from relocating when all samples are at distance 0 from center",
      "Reporter notes that with max_iter set very large or inf, KMeans would loop indefinitely"
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "Initialisation in the log is 'Initialization complete' with a single init (n_init reduced), but the init method is not stated in the passages apart from the regression test passing init=X explicitly",
      "Stopping criterion in the fixed behaviour is inferred from the regression test (n_iter_ == 1) and commit message, not from an explicit tolerance value",
      "Passages do not state dtype, precision, or a numeric convergence tolerance"
    ]
